Let $(K_i)_{i\ge 1}$ be a sequence of compact subsets of $\mathbb{R}$ satisfying:
(i) $0 \in K_i$ for every $i \ge 1$;
(ii) every element of every $K_i$ is nonnegative;
(iii) $\operatorname{diam}(K_i) > 0$ for every $i \ge 1$;
(iv) $\operatorname{diam}(K_i) \to 0$ as $i \to \infty$.

Define the achievement set
$$ S \;=\; \Big\{\, \sum_{j=1}^{\infty} x_j \;:\; x_j \in K_j \text{ for every } j \,\Big\} \subseteq \mathbb{R}, $$
and, for each integer $z \ge 0$, the tail set
$$ R_z \;=\; \Big\{\, \sum_{i=z+1}^{\infty} x_i \;:\; x_i \in K_i \text{ for every } i > z \,\Big\}. $$

Characterize, up to homeomorphism, all topological spaces that can arise as $S$ for some such sequence $(K_i)_{i\ge 1}$.

